@@ -53,0 +54,12 @@
+`style_reference` lists declared component and global stylesheets with exact
+hashes when available, and bounded selector-rule candidates for the element's
+literal tag, class, or ID. `LOCAL_COMPOUND_MATCH` relates a simple selector to
+the source declaration; `POSSIBLE_CONTEXT` requires an unverified ancestor,
+pseudo state, media context, or project scope. An inline CSS rule's `line` is
+relative to the CSS literal, with the component decorator line recorded
+separately. `UNKNOWN` lists missing stylesheets, imports, preprocessors,
+unsupported syntax, or bounds in `issues`; known rules are still returned.
+`BOUNDED_SOURCE` means all declared stylesheet source in this bounded scan was
+read and parsed. Neither state proves the effective cascade, active media
+query, inherited styles, computed style, missing-rule irrelevance, or geometry.
+
